[1mtack help[22m[2m · explore ·[22m[32m ✓ success[39m

Browse the catalog and edit one destination in an interactive
terminal. Without a flag it opens the project that contains the
current directory, or else the destination chooser; --project
and --user open that selection. Rows show each resource's state
in the destination. i, x and a stage an include, exclude or docs
attachment, and the same key again unstages it; u unstages and r
resets a saved pick to the source default. c reviews the staged
changes: picks and docs apply with a sync only after y, and a
profile save changes only its file and publication. d chooses
another destination: user, project, profile, or browse only.
Built-in daily selections are locked. Agents and non-interactive
callers are refused; use tack catalog, tack pick and tack
status.

  [2mUsage[22m  tack explore [flags]
  [2mMode[22m   conditional

[1mFlags[22m
  --project <string>  Select a registered project
  --user              Select the user namespace

[1mRoot flags[22m
  --json                Print the version 1 JSON envelope; only
                        status, sync, doctor, upgrade and
                        version have a stable payload
  --state-dir <string>  Override the Tack state directory

[1mExamples[22m
  [36mtack explore[39m
    [2mOpen the current project, or choose a destination[22m
  [36mtack explore --project demo[39m
    [2mStage picks and docs for demo, review the sync plan, then[22m
    [2mapply[22m
  [36mtack explore --user[39m
    [2mDo the same for the user namespace[22m
